  "rulesCheckersIntro": "An 8×8 board, 12 pieces each on dark squares. Men move forward diagonally and capture in any direction. Kings fly along the diagonal.",
  "rulesCheckersPlay": "Captures are mandatory. A king or man must keep capturing while a further jump is possible from the landing square — you cannot stop mid-sequence. If several directions are available, you may choose any of them; the longest capture is not required. A man that reaches the last rank becomes a king.",
  "rulesCheckersWin": "In Russian draughts you win by capturing all opposing pieces or leaving the opponent with no move. In giveaway the player who cannot move wins.",
  "rulesCheckersOfflineBot": "Offline: a game against the bot.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayRussian": "Russian draughts: 12 pieces each on dark squares. Men move diagonally forward and capture forward or backward. Kings fly any number of squares. Captures are mandatory: you must continue if another jump is possible, but you may choose any direction — not necessarily the longest. Win by capturing all enemy pieces or leaving the opponent with no moves.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayEnglish": "English draughts: 12 pieces each. Men move and capture only diagonally forward. Kings move one square diagonally in any direction. Captures are mandatory. Win by capturing all enemy pieces or leaving the opponent with no moves.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayGiveaway": "Giveaway: the same moves as Russian draughts, but the goal is reversed — lose all your pieces or be left with no moves. Captures are still mandatory.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayCorners": "Corners: pieces start in opposite corners. Move to an adjacent empty square horizontally or vertically, or jump over any piece without removing it. The goal is to move all your pieces into the opponent’s corner.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayCornersNoReturn": "A piece that has left its starting corner may not return there.",
  "rulesCheckersPlayCornersLeaveHome": "Pieces still in the home corner must leave it within the player’s first 25 moves.",
  "rulesCheckersDrawRussian": "A draw if the same position occurs three times, or if 15 moves by each side are only king moves without a capture — including two kings against two kings shuffling for no win.",
  "rulesCheckersDrawEnglish": "A draw if the same position occurs three times, if 40 moves pass without a capture or a man moving, or if only one king remains on each side.",
  "rulesCheckersDrawGiveaway": "A draw if the same position occurs three times, or if 15 moves by each side are only king moves without a capture — shuffling does not count as progress.",
  "rulesCheckersDrawCorners": "A draw if the same position occurs three times, or if 25 moves by each side add no extra pieces to the target corner.",
  "rulesChessPlayers": "Players: 2.",
  "rulesChessMode": "Mode: {mode}.",
  "rulesChessPlayClassic": "An 8×8 board. Each side has a king, queen, two rooks, two bishops, two knights and eight pawns. White moves first. The king moves one square, the queen along ranks, files and diagonals, the rook along ranks and files, the bishop on diagonals, the knight in an L. A pawn steps forward one square (two from its start), captures diagonally; en passant and promotion apply. Castling is allowed if the king and rook have not moved and the path is clear. Win by checkmate or if the opponent resigns.",
  "rulesChessDrawClassic": "A draw on stalemate, threefold repetition, the 50-move rule with no capture or pawn move, insufficient mating material, or by agreement.",
  "rulesChessClockClassic": "Game clock: 60+0 — 60 minutes for the whole game, no increment.",
